    "rationale": "Manual validation only; scripts could not be run in this environment. Present risk is driven by an untrusted third-party MCP server whose mutable tool definition directly instructs credential file access and external exfiltration, plus remembered approvals that do not act as real per-call gates. The most important decaying control is ctrl.first_call_approval, because once approval is remembered later sensitive calls are effectively ungated and model-summary framing is vulnerable to trust exploitation. Additional confidence limits come from missing source code and missing runtime observability details, but the core paths are evidenced directly by the provided MCP config, tool description, and runtime notes."
  },
